        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "Fabric dispatch — RunShape → Allocation → Receipt (GitHub is the queue, not the scheduler)",
        nodes: [
          authored_wi(id: "2-strictlease", done: false, content: "**StrictLease allocation model (Policy 0)** — every provider exposes strict, non-oversubscribed `RunShape` offers first: one allocation consumes its declared RAM/swap/CPU budget, period. srv1/srv2 are modeled like ephemeral providers (N fixed slots, hard cgroup caps, read-back receipts before work); Ubicloud is a provider offer with `EphemeralVm` isolation. Burst/oversubscription explicitly out of scope. Four nouns, no scheduler: `RunShape` (arch/cpu_tokens/ram/swap/disk/duration/trust/workload_class) · `ProviderOffer` (provider/isolation/limits/oversubscription_policy/cost) · `Allocation` (shape×offer→target+lease) · `Receipt` (effective limits observed, peak usage, pressure/OOM events, release result). **Accept ([checklist](docs/plans/fleet-acceptance-criteria.md)):** one real CI job runs under a `StrictLease` allocation on srv1/srv2 whose `Receipt` proves effective limits == the offer's declared limits (read back from the live cgroup, never asserted), and a second job requesting more than remaining capacity is refused a lease rather than co-scheduled.", intricacy: IntricacyHigh, volume: VolumeMedium, repo: "gunbc"),
          authored(id: "2-shape-labels", done: false, content: "**CI shape labels — `runs-on` as a projection of the fabric model** — `ci.yml` emits `runs-on` labels derived from `RunShape` (e.g. `gunbc-shape-ci-42c-128g`), never host names; the runner registration/converge layer ensures the right runners carry those labels. GitHub remains the queue and **runner availability is the backpressure**: register slots per shape at safe strict capacity (e.g. 2 `shape-rust-heavy` + more light), NOT 10 equivalent heavy runners when only 2 heavy jobs are safe. A fabric-control-plane allocator (a `.dag` control server minting leases/JIT runners before dispatch) is the LATER architecture — only after srv1/srv2 are safely mutable and readable."),
          authored(id: "2-provider-offer", done: false, content: "**ProviderOffer rows + the dormant-Ubicloud design-break probe** — srv1/srv2 fixed-host slots and Ubicloud ephemeral VMs inhabit the same offer type; add the Ubicloud row `Dormant` (16 vCPU/48GiB arm64, oversubscription: None) **without running it**. Acceptance = adding the offer changes no scheduler/control-plane invariant: witnesses prove (a) allocation accepts both `SrvHostSlot` and `UbicloudVmOffer`, (b) host-mutation code REFUSES Ubicloud offers (no cgroup target to mutate), (c) deploy-to-srv1 refuses `LocalShell` unless the allocation target proves host=srv1, (d) emitted labels encode shape, not provider host details. If adding Ubicloud forces a special case anywhere, the abstraction is wrong — this probe answers \"does our design break?\" before it can cost anything."),
          authored(id: "2-burstlease", done: false, content: "**BurstLease (Policy 1) — oversubscription earned by receipts** — co-resident allocations on one host only after pressure/OOM/swap receipts prove the measured peaks allow it; StrictLease stays the default and the fallback. This is where stranded cores come back (sessions, compression, IO, smaller jobs) — on 128c/125GiB, strict memory allocation strands CPU and that is correct: **the first goal is non-death, not full utilization**. Gated on the sound-host-admission receipts and the live read seam."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "2-shape-labels"), parent: nid(s: "2-strictlease") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "2-provider-offer"), parent: nid(s: "2-strictlease") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "2-burstlease"), parent: nid(s: "2-provider-offer") },
        ],
      ),
      section_prose(content: "**Ordering (operator-signed):** ① CD target-host proof → ② stateless-frontend MVP receipt (milestone A, on the existing deploy path) → ③ live read seam + privilege model → ④ one converge hunk closed-loop end-to-end (the narrow srv2 acceptance case) → ⑤ service allocation generalized from the frontend MVP → ⑥ StrictLease + shape labels; register srv1/srv2 slots by shape → ⑦ dormant Ubicloud row proves no design break → ⑧ CI jobs move to shape labels → ⑨ receipts (effective limits · peaks · OOM/swap pressure) → ⑩ BurstLease / dynamic routing / richer placement. ①–④ make infra changeable (everything else is paper until then); ⑤ proves the fabric is not just CI; ⑥ fixes backpressure with no scheduler; ⑦ validates the abstraction before we depend on it; ⑧–⑨ make CI consume the model; ⑩ recovers stranded cores."),
      section_group(
        label: "Fleet hardening — make our metal safe for the load it carries",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "2-fleet-hardening", done: false, content: "**the return happened ungated** — #6111 put required CI back on srv1/srv2 by operator call, accepting interim OOM/sccache exposure; the items below are the gates the return *should* have had, now owed as hardening. Ubicloud remains the burst/fallback offer (and the slot-shape template the admission model generalizes)."),
          authored(id: "2-session-slice", done: false, content: "**SessionSliceEnforcement + verified-effective caps** — agent-session cgroups have no citable verified-effective cap (the residual over-commit vector on srv1/srv2); the humming apply-rule stands: runner caps must not tighten while sessions are uncapped and oomd is absent."),
          authored_doc(id: "2-oom-consumer", done: false, content: "**OOM classification consumer** — `ClusteredOutOfMemoryKill` is modeled but absent from the active infra-retry signature roster; build the consumer so an OOM is first-class, never EAGAIN-shaped.", path: "docs/plans/ci-oom-reclassification.md"),
          authored(id: "1-sched-resource-aware", done: false, content: "**resource-aware scheduler (implementation)** — implements the signed [bounded-input / cost-envelope scheduling](docs/plans/bounded-input-cost-envelope-scheduling.md) design: (A) per-shard peak-RSS plumbing → (B) `Runnable.cost` with Predicted `CostEnvelope` → (C) scheduler reads cost, static side-channel deleted → (D) Measured falsifies Predicted, calibration loop retires data rows (#5431 instrument). Construction invariant: more memory → more width → more throughput, no `.dag` edits. [tracker](docs/plans/resource-aware-scheduler.md)"),
          authored_pp(id: "1-budget-tree", done: false, content: "**resource budget tree** — admission (construction) · conserve-lens (honest residue) · runtime reconcile (fail-closed handler), three verdicts never conflated; subsumes spawn-width/placement/compile-jobs as consumer leaves. Protective only when paired with an enforcement actuator (cgroup `memory.max`, operator-fenced).", carriers: [ptr(label: "carrier", path: "dag/product/budget_tree.dag"), ptr(label: "grounding", path: "docs/plans/budget-tree.md")]),
          authored(id: "1-placement-authority", done: false, content: "**one Placement authority** — jobs (GitHub) · threads (`spawn_width`) · sessions (ctrl capacity) are 3 forks of \"put work on a host\"; `Placement`/`Materialization` are modeled but inert — CI consuming them is the lane's real deliverable."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "2-session-slice"), parent: nid(s: "2-fleet-hardening") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "2-oom-consumer"), parent: nid(s: "2-fleet-hardening") },
        ],
      ),
    ],
  }
}

fn section_3() -> RoadmapSection {
  RoadmapSection {
    title: "3. The floor — audit what we have (does it actually do what it claims?)",
    elements: [
      section_prose(content: "Both pillars ride the CI floor: tree-wide marker-driven witness discovery · compile-clean gate · generated-artifact drift gates (this document is one) · `regen --verify` (#5873) · doc-graph reachability · emit-determinism (#5941) · the interim self-host comparison (#6009). Those stand. The floor's *expansion* lanes (testgen, wiring-liveness, complexity gates, lens meta-walls) are shelved — a new wall must displace a measured cost on a pillar path to un-shelve (the **enforcement-intent gate** below is the first such un-shelve, 2026-07-02: displaced cost = the operator's repeated manual *what-is-enforced-by-what-lens-over-what-corpus* join, plus CI-killing quadratics and repeated dual-representation/anemia rediscovery)."),
      section_prose(content: "**Audit directive (operator, 2026-07-01): thoroughly audit what we have and what it actually does.** For each load-bearing mechanism, prove **by execution** that it does what it claims, with a **discriminating perturb** that goes RED when the behavior is wrong — a typecheck or a grep is not a consumer (DESIGN §5), and a wired gate can still be vacuous. A mechanism claim without a red-control is *unverified*, whatever its docs say. The reset's own mapping found the pattern live: the committed converge shell is spec-without-execution (§2), the fixpoint gate self-declares interim (2-of-92 files), cargo-green is an ignored test. Highest-stakes mechanisms first:"),
      section_group(
        label: "Audit — green by execution, red by perturbation",
        nodes: [
          authored_wi(id: "3-audit-affected-set", done: false, content: "**affected-set lens** *(the operator's named example)* — witness-level skip is LIVE on the floor (#6061); prove it: (a) **soundness** — construct a diff that MUST re-run a witness and assert it runs (a skipped-but-affected witness is the fail-open catastrophe); (b) **effectiveness** — receipts on real scoped diffs (skip counts + wall-clock delta, not claims); (c) **fail-closed default** — a provenance gap falls back to run-all, witnessed RED-on-perturb. The node-closure half (#6105) inherits the same receipt obligation before it may prune.", intricacy: IntricacyHigh, volume: VolumeMedium, repo: "gunbc"),
          sign(rn: owned(rn: with_plan(rn: authored_wi(id: "3-audit-gate-inventory", done: true, content: "**mechanism inventory with red-controls** — census every wired gate/lens/cache (floor-plan roster + `commit_workflow`): what it claims · its discriminating RED witness · its last execution receipt. Anything without a red-control gets one or gets demoted/deleted. The inert-lens backstop (#5433) covers *wiring*; this covers *claim-vs-behavior*.", intricacy: IntricacyMedium, volume: VolumeLarge, repo: "gunbc"), path: "docs/plans/mechanism-inventory-red-controls.md"), owner: "dispatched 2026-07-01 · adhoc-c67edbed-916"), s: signed(by: "operator", works: true, scope_equivalent: true, as_expected: true)),
          authored(id: "3-audit-cache-honesty", done: false, content: "**cache honesty re-receipt** — re-run the warm==cold purity oracle against CURRENT main (616/616 was pre-reset), and close the sccache exit-0-no-binary class (below); a cache that lies is worse than no cache."),
          authored_wi(id: "3-audit-artifact-freshness", done: false, content: "**artifact-freshness gate** *(operator ask: \"we need a freshness gate, if we don't already have one\")* — we half-do: the per-PR drift gate proves committed==emitted for the PR's OWN tree, but drift still LANDED on main (`.gitignore` stale vs its authority since #6097; found and healed by #6110/#6111) because admission never re-validates against CURRENT main — green-on-branch is not green-on-main. The closing mechanism is the §2 merge-admission freshness block (HELD); this item is its receipt pair: (a) reproduce the landed-drift path as a RED witness, (b) confirm the freshness block refuses it once un-HELD.", intricacy: IntricacyMedium, volume: VolumeSmall, repo: "gunbc"),
          authored(id: "3-audit-gate-disagreement", done: false, content: "**one tree, one verdict** — 2026-07-01 live finding: `dag_compile_clean_gate` was GREEN while the discovery-corpus resolve of the same tree was RED (`extdeps.shell` module collision, silent last-root-wins shadowing; de-fork + loud-collision wall shipped as the hotfix). Two resolve paths gave two verdicts on one corpus — enumerate every place a module index is built, and make their collision/ordering semantics ONE authority so a gate cannot be green on a tree the floor cannot resolve."),
          authored(id: "3-enforcement-intent", done: false, content: "**enforcement intent + model-quality walls** *(operator-directed 2026-07-02; §3 un-shelve — displaced cost: repeated manual \"what is enforced, by what lens, over what corpus\" joins; CI-killing quadratics; repeated dual-representation/anemia rediscovery)* — model the operator's recurring standing directives as durable `StandingIntent` rows and gate the relationship (intent ⇄ `LensContract` ⇄ `CoverageReceipt`) fail-closed, so a mechanism *claiming* enforcement is complete only when the gate proves the claim **from receipts, not self-declared contract claims**. One new authority (`StandingIntent`); everything else extends existing machinery (`LensRegistryEntryV0` → `LensContract`; reuse `ConstructionJustification` / `subject_roster`; consume `intent_linearity` / `self_applying_lenses`). Anti-overcomplication: no lens may claim *repo-wide* / *blocking* / *complete* / *self-applying* unless the gate can prove it. Rollout: rows live; gate Blocking on contract consistency; object rules AuditOnly until receipts land. Children, A→C before object rules D/E: **A** StandingIntent carrier + LensContract extension (`ConsumerKind`/`ConsumerRequirement` NOT hardwired to `FloorGate`; `EnforcementMode` order `Advisory < AuditOnly < Blocking` modeled) · **B** enforcement_intent_gate contract-consistency reds (over `CoverageReceipt`s) · **C** complexity.repo-wide first proof (3 legs red today, no `decl_facts` dep) · **D** complexity R1 accumulator-in-copied-port object rule (HOLDS behind #6155) · **E** anemia/consolidation first model-quality consumers (suggest a consolidation target, not just warn). [design](docs/plans/enforcement-intent-design.md)"),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "Cost / risk / benefit — the floor's unmodeled optimization",
        nodes: [
          authored_pp(id: "3-cost-risk-benefit", done: false, content: "**model cost/risk/benefit — \"what do we actually run\" is one optimization, not a pile of policies** *(operator working session 2026-07-12)* — affected-set, wet/dry (mocks), receipt/`long`, `ReadsLiveTree` never-skip, and the test-kind names (`test`/`receipt`/`demo`/`integration`, `WitnessKind`, `TestClassification`) are all **unmodeled proxies** for `argmax(benefit − cost)` under a budget — hand-tuned stand-ins (mostly astrology) that exist because cost/risk/benefit were never first-class. Root anemia: `test fn` bakes in `cost ≈ 0, run always`, which is false (`s1_closure` ≈ 10min wet). **Invariant that keeps it fail-closed:** you may trade fidelity for cost (mocks, skips, deferrals), but the risk you trade away must stay **observable on a cadence** — deferred-and-detected, never silent (§5; a silent widen is the absorbing fallback). This inverts the tree's current *wet-is-sacred* default: wet is just the highest-cost fidelity point, usually not worth it. **Bootstrappable now:** a claim's expected internal work is inspectable (inputs/expected-output node shape) and its effects enumerable (which service ops, how many times via fold/loop bounds), each effect carrying a latency expectation; the floor already MEASURES `wall_nanos`/cgroup-peak per claim, so cost = measured receipt now → graph-derived later (§4). **Landed as approximation in #6506 (Stages 0–2):** hermetic-by-default floor, a flat hand-set **5s** per-witness budget (fail-closed `EvalBudgetExceeded`), and a `test/claim/long/` cadence — right shape, interim stand-ins; forward work is Stages 3–5. **Missing pieces (highlighted, not papered over):** no per-effect cost model; cost only bounded by the flat 5s budget, not derived from the graph (fail-closed = expensive on unknown fold bounds); the budget is flat/hand-set, not a per-run wall-clock allocated by value/cost; **benefit unmodeled** — only footholds are the §5 lower bound (no discriminating red ⟹ ~0 gate-value ⟹ drop, this is what a pure `demo` is) and observed red-frequency; the proxies aren't yet reconciled to the axes. **Sequence:** cost first (compute/resources, from what's measurable now) with budget-aware admission and *counted typed deferrals* (never silent skip) → benefit second (§5 lower bound + red-frequency, declared interim for the rest) → then affected-set/wet-dry/cadence/test-kinds collapse into derived readings and the qualitative vocabulary is deleted, not extended.", carriers: [ptr(label: "cost/risk/benefit model", path: "docs/plans/cost-risk-benefit-floor-model.md")]),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "Open floor holes",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "1-nightly", done: false, content: "**nightly full-corpus selector-backstop** — per-PR selection is only sound because nightly runs everything; ⚠ CI-gen load-bearing"),
          authored_pp(id: "1-builtin-registry", done: false, content: "**tree-scoped builtin registry** (fail-closed) — the global seed registry leaks intrinsics into the substrate compile, making compile-clean falsely green; instance fix #5452, class fix (partition) open", carriers: [ptr(label: "force-check plan", path: "docs/plans/compile-clean-forcecheck.md")]),
          authored(id: "1-sccache-falsegreens", done: false, content: "**kill sccache false-greens** — exit-0-no-binary; build-verify asserts the artifact exists + is fresh (partly landed in `ci.yml`)"),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
    ],
  }
}

fn section_4() -> RoadmapSection {
  RoadmapSection {
    title: "4. Shelved (parked 2026-07-01 — not deleted)",
    elements: [
      section_prose(content: "Every lane below was live roadmap before the reset. Shelved = plan docs and carriers stay in place, nothing dispatches from here, and the git-history ROADMAP.md holds the full pre-reset detail (structure, milestones, sign-off states). Un-shelve by PR into §1–§3, priced in displaced cost. **(2026-07-06: the *complexity budget whole-codebase*, *fail-closed meta band*, and *fold-ergonomics* lanes are un-shelved into §0's priority order ② and ⑤ — this reshuffle is that PR; their nodes stay catalogued here until relocated into their §2/§3 lanes.)**"),
      section_group(
        label: "",
        nodes: [
          plain(id: "shelf-ergonomics", content: "**fold-ergonomics lane** — inert-abstraction lens · non-fold-residue audit · staging combinator · ban source comments [charter](docs/plans/fold-ergonomics.md) [residue catalogue](docs/plans/non-fold-irreducible-residue-catalogue.md) [debt sample audit](docs/plans/real-debt-syntactic-sample-audit.md) [eval-bind PROPOSE](docs/plans/eval-bind-node-eval-propose.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-failclosed-meta", content: "**fail-closed meta band** — `Value::Null` split (the deep root) · Disposition carrier · reference grounding · cardinality refinement · expressibility frontier · reachability-completeness lens · axiom+syllogism lens · self-applying lenses · inert-lens promotion + gate-hygiene residue [lockdown](docs/plans/fail-closed-lockdown.md) [fork plan](docs/plans/model-realization-fork.md) [Disposition](docs/plans/disposition-carrier.md) [reference grounding](docs/plans/reference-grounding-migration.md) [cardinality](docs/plans/cardinality-refinement.md) [P1 where-lowering](docs/plans/p1-where-clause-lowering.md) [frontier](docs/plans/expressibility-frontier.md) [inert-layer lens](docs/plans/inert-layer-lens.md) [axiom lens](docs/plans/axiom-syllogism-lens.md) [self-applying](docs/plans/self-applying-lenses.md) [construction rule](docs/plans/construction-justification-rule.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-rust-gate", content: "**rust-gate `.dag`→rust coverage wall (edge-b)** + stage0 clone-census ratchet [brief](docs/plans/edge-b-rust-dag-provenance-brief.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-complexity", content: "**complexity budget whole-codebase** + the algebraic-rewrite construction engine (O(n²)→O(n) catalog, `Unknown` dissolution) [rewrite plan](docs/plans/algebraic-rewrite-optimization.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-testgen", content: "**testgen oracle + wiring-liveness family** (compile-time wiring lens ✓ #5679 · pre-send guard ✓ #5683 stand; the generator/preflight expansion parks) [method](docs/plans/testgen-oracle.md) [wiring](docs/plans/wiring-liveness-preflight.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-caching-completion", content: "**caching completion** — `realize(subject)` one door (P2) · M5 fixture-store · native `content(T)` (P5) · B1 generic-instantiation / B2 cross-tree content-hash blockers · one Materialization kernel · shared secrets model [loop](docs/plans/realization-measurement-loop.md) [M4](docs/plans/m4-universal-hermetic-corpus.md) [M5](docs/plans/m5-fixture-store-consolidation.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-deforks-small", content: "**CI inline-shell de-fork · interpreter terminal-output de-fork** (seed forks of modeled authorities; both shrink as v1 burns down) [emission-ingestion](docs/plans/emission-ingestion-inverse.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-idea-machine", content: "**idea machine** — ingest-at-large · English closure/round-trip · cross-media (JSON/react/diagram) · `Medium` homomorphisms · format-model C4–C6 · fidelity compose-up · eval generalization · invert-hand-maintained residue [plan](docs/plans/idea-machine.md) [format reconciliation](docs/plans/format-model-reconciliation.md) [invert](docs/plans/invert-hand-maintained.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-shell-tail", content: "**shell-emission slices 3–4 (census-rescoped)** — live_deploy → thin-run/typed-effect candidate (runtime-present; not a golden to freeze) · bmc_token_federation (two Do rows) → ci_workflow RunSteps → githooks thin shim [plan](docs/plans/shell-emission-model.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-typescript", content: "**TypeScript first-class emit + TS self-host** — END GOAL UNCHANGED (both realizations, per plan do-not-relitigate); resumes after the Rust fixed point [gap census](docs/plans/typescript-gap-census.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-language-frontier", content: "**language-target self-host frontier** — the get-to-self-host path for all emission languages (Rust as model; Verilog/SPICE/LLVM as design-stress falsifiers); solve resolved as higher-order not a primitive [frontier](docs/plans/language-target-self-host-frontier.md) [solve rationale](docs/plans/solve-higher-order-design.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-html-dashboard", content: "**HTML/React + live dashboard lane** — page ✓ (#6010) and srv1 deploy ✓ (#6030) keep running as-is; interactivity · idea-input · demo park. The minimal **stateless-frontend fabric slice is active in §2** only as a storage+compute+route consumer, not as the full dashboard/product lane (the CD *transport* fix is also §2 live work)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-session-dashboard", content: "**session dashboard + roadmap-as-spawner** — the *automatic* spawn bridge stays fail-closed paused; §1–§3 sized nodes are the only dispatch surface (§3 audit items are deliberately dispatchable — the operator's audit lanes). The operator-clicked **dispatch actuator** slice is un-shelved into §2 (2026-07-03) [plan](docs/plans/roadmap-spawner.md)"),
          plain(id: "shelf-gunbhub", content: "**gunbhub** (own the Git/CI engine, closes G6) · internal repo model · compute fabric as a sellable piece"),
          plain(id: "shelf-privacy", content: "**privacy / isolation model for the compute fabric** — trust boundaries, tenant isolation, what the fabric may observe about a workload; was compute-fabric downstream work pre-reset, parked here so it is not lost (`trust_class` on `RunShape` is its active §2 seam). Includes committed-secret references (operator 2026-07-02, not urgent): a typed `SecretRef` — GCP Secret Manager resource name + version/content-hash — so sensitive facts (router serial, WAN MAC, public prefixes, credentials) commit as model-legible references while values stay in Secret Manager; redaction by construction (public shapes carry no raw-value field); first consumer: the network-identity observation fixtures."),
          plain(id: "shelf-structural-walls", content: "**structural correctness walls (standing, not active)** — generated-output gate · coproduct exhaustiveness · cross-representation equality · oracle-method map; they keep gating, no expansion work dispatches from here"),
          plain(id: "shelf-sketches", content: "**design sketches without an active lane** [orchestration-as-intent](docs/plans/orchestration-as-intent-design.md) [model-grounding extract](docs/plans/model-grounding-lens-extract.md) [node-minimal representation](docs/plans/node-minimal-representation-sketch.md) [func-env sigs](docs/plans/func-env-sigs-single-authority.md) [resolved-graph minimization](docs/plans/resolved-graph-representation-minimization.md) [emit-host batch isolation](docs/plans/emit-host-batch-isolation.md) [accelerator roundtrip](docs/plans/accelerator-demo-roundtrip.md) [commit workflow](docs/plans/commit-workflow.md) [input envelope](docs/plans/input-envelope-roadmap.md) [seed-debt bundle 2](docs/plans/seed-debt-bundle-item-2.md) [resolver collision wall](docs/plans/resolver-type-name-collision-wall.md) [regime-2 shared emission](docs/plans/regime2-shared-emission-fold.md)"),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
    ],
  }
}

fn task_sheet_lead_lane() -> RoadmapSection {
  RoadmapSection {
    title: "Operator TODO — consolidated (2026-07-22 · CI audit + merge wave)",
    elements: [
      section_prose(content: "The operator's real TODO, organized (2026-07-22): six numbered items, each grounded in the lanes that already exist — pointers dispatch work, rows track it. Each row points at its carrier (PR · branch · issue · lane node); check a row when its lane merges or its issue closes, delete it when the pointer goes stale. DISSOLUTION: this lane is a dated scaffold — delete it when every row is checked or re-homed into §1–§4."),
      section_group(
        label: "1 · Main to actual green (audit receipts, 2026-07-22)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-falsifier-nfr", done: true, content: "**falsifier dark since 2026-07-16 — roster burn-down** — every 4-hourly cold run red on `non_fold_residue_clean_holds` + `non_fold_residue_no_unrostered_or_stale`, logged as predicted=unaffected / actual=red divergences. Root-caused 2026-07-22 by local receipt (`nfr_roster_receipt`): 3 unrostered sites, 0 stale — `dag/gunbc/host_converge_slice1.dag::host_converge_slice1_host_result_all_valid` + `::host_converge_slice1_host_result_applied_count` (landed #7009) and `dag/gunbc/host_hygiene_reaper.dag::action_kills_build_cache_server` (landed #7026). LANDED with this sheet update: the 3 roster rows (reason + dissolution trigger each, the #6691 shape) are in `cli_run.rs`; receipt `nfr_roster_receipt` unrostered=0 stale=0 and the lens fn evaluates true by execution. The falsifier goes green on its next scheduled run and #7032 auto-closes — if it reds on anything else, that is a NEW find, not this one."),
          authored(id: "ts-deploy-tail", done: false, content: "**srv1 deploy keeps breaking and reds main while the floor is green** — 13 of 2026-07-22's 21 main-run failures are `deploy_dashboard_srv1`, not the floor: `gunbc-tree-sync.service` restart control-process failure (fix in flight: `session/sunny-owl-513`, receipt run 29928424523) after earlier `gunbc-roadmap.service` /healthz ServiceNotReady. Two halves: converge the srv1 units, and decide whether the deploy verdict should share the ci run's conclusion — main-green must mean code-green. The deeper fix is §2's CD-transport node; note `gunbc-roadmap.service` is also item 3's dispatch surface, so this fix is its prerequisite. UPDATE 2026-07-22 late: both halves of the unit fix are in — the tree-sync fix (16:34) and #7077's measured readiness bound (30s→120s; four srv1 starts at 35–39s prove the old bound red every SUCCESSFUL start). The tail executes for the first time on the first main run whose floor passes (post-#7080); check this row off on the first green deploy job, and keep the verdict-sharing question open. FIRST EXECUTIONS (21:49–21:50, both red, DIFFERENT causes — receipts from runs 29957321270/29957141552): (a) the #7077 run died at tree-sync — the .git/ rsync exited 23 (partial transfer) while a SECOND deploy job ran concurrently 18s later on another runner slot against the same /opt/gunbc target; deploy jobs have no concurrency group and ran out of commit order (newer commit deployed first, older second — even on success srv1 converges to the OLDER tree, last-writer-wins). NEW work: serialize the deploy (workflow concurrency group or host-side lock) and stop rsyncing .git/ from a live reusable runner checkout — the CD-transport node's case sharpens. (b) the #7080 run got past tree-sync, restarted the unit (active, 34s into its ~35–39s startup) and probed with the OLD 30s bound — its tree predates #7077; the known class, already fixed. The first honest 120s-bound deploy is the next main run carrying both fixes (#7058 merge, in flight at write time). THIRD EXECUTION (run 29961193892, 22:51): floor green a THIRD consecutive time, deploy red AGAIN at the same tree-sync .git rsync exit 23 — with NO concurrent deploy this time, which RECLASSIFIES the failure from race to a deterministic per-source-checkout condition: succeeded from srv1-03's checkout (21:49), failed twice from srv1-05's (21:49, 22:51). Leading suspect: service-user-unreadable files inside the runner checkout's .git/ (the oneshot reads ghrunner's checkout as User=service-user; a 0600 .git/config carrying the actions auth extraheader would explain exit 23 exactly — and note syncing .git/config to /opt/gunbc would be a CREDENTIAL LEAK if it ever succeeded, so excluding config from the .git sync is both the likely fix and a hardening). LOUDNESS gap, same class the status-tail was added for: the diagnosis shows exit 23 but never the per-file rsync errors (they live in the unit journal) — extend the capture to a journalctl tail so the failing paths are NAMED. The 120s readiness bound remains unexercised until tree-sync converges. RESOLUTION 2026-07-22 late: journal receipt named the root — ONE ghrunner-owned 0600 fetch marker (objects/pack/pack-25d0…keep) unreadable to the unit principal, deterministic on srv1-05; AND /opt/gunbc/gunbc/.git/config was carrying an actions extraheader auth token from the blanket sync (a real credential leak). Operator hand-scrubbed the token and removed the stale marker; the construction fix (whitelist .git sync — HEAD, objects minus fetch transients, packed-refs, refs, terminal exclude wall) MERGED with #7086, making both classes unwritable. Dashboard STAYS on srv1 (operator decision 2026-07-22); the srv3 move was assessed — redeploy-not-migration, ~1–2 days via HostIdentity spec parameterization shared with #7027 G1, plus service-account + claude-auth seeding — and parked."),
          authored(id: "ts-native-flip-revert", done: false, content: "**first NativeRouted flip reverted by receipt — the frontier working as designed** — main run 29963619401 (#7069 merge, srv2-05) redded `emit_on_demand_family_crate_pr_native_agreement_holds` WARM (compile_skipped=true ×3, false in 496ms): a genuine native-vs-eval divergence or member-run failure, NOT cold cache. Remedy per design: complement + meet_join back to `InterpretedRetained agreement_red_on_main` — a two-row data edit, receipt on the carrier (`routed_flip_reverted_note`), investigation off the merge-critical path, falsifier cold control still exercising both legs. Named loudness gap to close BEFORE re-flip: the agreement fn's false carries no located member and no value pair — a divergence receipt must name which member and both answers."),
          authored(id: "ts-queue", done: false, content: "**queue + zombie hygiene** — ~18 runs/hour arriving against a 60–97-min green wall; main pushes queue behind PR traffic; cancel zombie queued run 50073 (`session/clever-hawk-862`, queued 2026-07-13); revisit main-push priority."),
          authored(id: "ts-overnight", done: true, content: "**overnight main floor breakage healed** — the 00:44–02:04 cluster (DAG compile failure + ci_deploy_sudoers typecheck) was fixed on main by ~02:04; recorded so the day's red accounting separates it from the deploy-tail reds."),
          authored(id: "ts-roadmap-drift", done: true, content: "**ROADMAP.md hand-edit drift healed** — #7071 hand-added its §0 lane-snapshot paragraph to the generated ROADMAP.md without touching `roadmap_authority.dag`, leaving main committed ≠ expected (the drift gate reds whenever it executes). Re-homed verbatim into the authority in this change; the open question — why the per-PR floor let a generated-artifact hand edit through — folds into the predict-skip row in item 2."),
          authored(id: "ts-wave-reds", done: true, content: "**merge-wave floor reds root-caused and hotfixed** — the 16:11–17:31 wall of 15 main failures had two roots: (a) `generated_artifact_drift_gate` red from #7071 hand-editing the generated ROADMAP.md (healed by #7081 re-homing the paragraph), and (b) a stale `CommitWitnessClaim` roster row in `gunbc.commit_workflow` still enrolling the witness #7060 had moved to the long lane — every main run from 16:33Z failed with no-main-function-found (hotfixed #7079, which also cleared #7064 orphaned script-module import). THIRD collision: #7079 (branch cut before #7081) hand-deleted the same paragraph from the generated md as its own drift cleanup, so post-merge main drifts the OPPOSITE way — authority has the paragraph, committed md does not; #7082 closed it by regeneration (the freshness-block class exactly: green-on-branch is not green-on-main). Remaining for a green main push: the deploy tail verifies on the next run that reaches it, and the falsifier needs the nfr roster burn-down above."),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "1a · Host state frontier — machines are stateful; declare the boundary (operator, 2026-07-22)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-host-state", done: false, content: "**the gap, named**: our deploy/subsumption workflows are causal scripts over host state we neither guarantee nor model — and host state IS effectively infinitely permutable, so any workflow whose correctness depends on unmodeled state is untenable. The doctrine already half-exists (membership-reconcile observe→diff→converge, gunbc.ownership, fail-closed observation à la belt_observe); the gap is that THE BOUNDARY OF THE MODELED STATE IS UNDECLARED — both 2026-07-22 tail incidents happened exactly there (reading foreign state without a contract: the runner checkout's live .git; blanket-copying foreign state into owned state: the leaked extraheader). Resolution is NOT model-everything (observe-all is the absorbing trap in reverse) — it is shrink-the-state-that-matters: content-addressed desired state + idempotent converge + readback, so accumulated host state becomes irrelevant wherever the spine applies. Children are the three mechanisms."),
          authored(id: "ts-host-frontier", done: false, content: "**declared state frontier per host-touching workflow** — every state input/output classified `Derived` (regenerable from spec; delete-and-recreate always legal) | `OwnedMember` (observed + reconciled by identity — the membership spine) | `ForeignWithContract` (someone else's process, read only through a NAMED contract); unclassified refuses. The tree-sync whitelist (#7086) is the case study: an implicit read of all of .git became a four-item declared contract — but by incident, not at authoring time. This is the Group-of-units taxonomy (5a) applied to host state; extends gunbc.ownership."),
          authored(id: "ts-host-antientropy", done: false, content: "**anti-entropy cadence — the host falsifier** — drift is currently found only when a deploy trips on it (the stale .keep sat for weeks). Mirror the affected-set falsifier: a scheduled pass re-observes every enrolled member vs desired (readback) plus unowned-state-inside-owned-subtrees detection (would have caught the leaked config AND the stale server.js), divergences typed/located/counted. Seeds exist: host_hygiene_reaper, live_deploy readback."),
          authored(id: "ts-host-cdtransport", done: false, content: "**CD transport — stop deploying from a live runner workspace** — the shared root of both tail incidents: the runner checkout is a maximally stateful foreign entity and rsync-from-it is state coupling by construction. Deploy from the merged commit's CONTENT (fetch-by-hash from a store, or a clean host-side git fetch) — the whitelist narrowed the foreign-state contract; CD transport deletes it. Elevates §2's existing CD-transport node with this week's receipts."),
          authored(id: "ts-host-genlease", done: false, content: "**generation guard + subtree lease** — ordering and interference for concurrent effects on one host: apply refuses when the candidate desired-state is an ancestor of what is deployed (`StaleDesiredState` — the SAME refusal class as §2 merge-admission freshness: an effect admitted against observation O refuses if the world advanced past O — one authority, two consumers), and an effectful realization holds an exclusive write lease on its target subtree for the frame duration (effect-grants ⊑, modeled — not a shell flock). Interim: a workflow concurrency group on the deploy job (receipt: 21:49 two deploys overlapped, out of commit order)."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-host-frontier"), parent: nid(s: "ts-host-state") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-host-antientropy"), parent: nid(s: "ts-host-state") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-host-cdtransport"), parent: nid(s: "ts-host-state") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-host-genlease"), parent: nid(s: "ts-host-state") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "2 · CI actually functional — what it takes, what the roadmap already claims",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-ci-definition", done: false, content: "**definition — CI is functional when (a) a red means a real defect, (b) a green is trustworthy corpus-wide, and (c) the verdict arrives before merge.** Today none of the three hold: deploy reds mask code health (item 1), predict-skip hides corpus reds until the falsifier, and merges land 0–17 min after open while a green run takes 60–97 min."),
          authored(id: "ts-lying-stamp", done: false, content: "**kill the recurrence class — corpus-scan witnesses predict-skipped** — 4th occurrence per the nfr roster's own dated blocks: hygiene witnesses stamped `SubstrateInputsOnly` while their counters walk the whole corpus, so per-PR selection skips them and only the falsifier reds, days later. Decide once: re-stamp `ReadsLiveTree` (never-predict-skip; sub-ms at floor scale) vs falsifier-red as a merge blocker. Census machinery landed #7070."),
          authored(id: "ts-merge-gate", done: false, content: "**CI is not a merge gate (re-evidence)** — 0–17-minute creation→merge latencies observed in the merge wave while a green run takes 60+ min, so verdicts land post-merge and main is the integration testbed; re-evidences §2's merge-admission HELD-state node — while it stays HELD and the falsifier is dark, the corpus has no pre-merge wall at all."),
          authored(id: "ts-floor-memory", done: false, content: "**floor memory ceiling** — falsifier floor pinned at the 16 GiB cgroup memory.high with ~33 GB swap, sustained PSI stalls, and ~18 min of post-failure residual burn; #7000 (srv3 MemoryHigh/MemoryMax caps) landed 2026-07-22 — confirm the next falsifier runs reflect the caps; residual lineage #6848 → #7030."),
          authored(id: "ts-ci-claimed", done: false, content: "**already claimed in the roadmap — dispatch from these lanes, do not re-plan them**: §0 ① compile wall + ③ affected-set live in CI; §2 floor-throughput group (serial compile-clean wall · shard A ✓ / shard B · within-run double-resolve · resolve-cache default-on) targeting floor <1min; §2 workload-class admission + cap/admission de-conflation; §3 audit rows (affected-set soundness receipts · one tree one verdict · cache honesty re-receipt); the CI-onto-v2 native-routing lane (#7069, parity-gated). What the audit adds is only sequencing: falsifier green first (item 1), then selection honesty, then speed — a fast CI that lies is worse than a slow one."),
          authored(id: "ts-ci-options", done: false, content: "**the merge-gate options — pick one deliberately**: (i) GitHub-required check + merge queue, once the floor is fast enough to gate (needs §2 floor-throughput); (ii) keep post-merge CI but close §2 merge-admission — freshness block un-HELD — so admission is modeled rather than GitHub-native; (iii) interim, available today: falsifier-red blocks merges by convention. Doing none is the current state, and the last two weeks are its receipt."),
          authored(id: "ts-ci-ergonomics", done: false, content: "**CI ergonomics — the operator loop is clunky (operator, 2026-07-22)** — using CI today means digging raw run logs for the red witness, hand-correlating roster/selection/receipt state, ad-hoc local claim_batch incantations, and minutes-to-hours of latency before any signal. Open the lane by inventorying the operator touchpoints and pricing each (§6 displaced cost): where is the red — one link from the PR to the failing witness and its receipt, never a log dig · one local command == CI floor (same selection, same receipts) · floor/falsifier/deploy state visible at a glance (a dashboard tile on the srv1 roadmap — rides item 3 serving surface) · re-run and bisect ergonomics (re-kick one witness, not the whole floor). Existing machinery to feed on: logs-on-failure #7055, the gantt/receipt emissions, the belt dashboard."),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "2a · Witness corpus onto v2-native — the bulk arc (operator re-priced 2026-07-22)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-native-bulk", done: false, content: "**the arc: rail → census → seams → one bulk flip PR.** Today 0% of the ~2,200-witness corpus executes native — all of it runs through the v1 interpreter (~30 of the 41-min ci job). Operator re-pricing (2026-07-22): parity windows demote from flip-precondition to post-flip monitoring — no customers, so a divergence should land immediately and loudly, never drip-feed. The in-PR receipt is ONE agreement run (both legs, hard equality), and a native-vs-interpreted disagreement FAILS THE FLOOR loudly — never a counted-and-continue row (the §5 wall that replaces the windows). Cache posture: staleness is a cache-key bug with a standing detector (the 4-hourly falsifier cold control, unchanged), not a reason to fear the cache; R2 (real toolchain identity in the `.native_ready` key) rides #7069 and lands before the flip. Sizing (sharp-bee-290, 2026-07-22): ~4–6 working days after #7069 merges; owner session started by operator."),
          authored(id: "ts-native-census", done: false, content: "**eligibility census — measure, never guess**: grain is the ENTRY CLOSURE — 744 entry files (337 dag/test/claim + 407 src/v2/test/claim), not 2,200 witnesses. Hard ceiling ~90%: 77 ReadsLiveTree + 35 host-effect entries stay InterpretedRetained host_fed — native host-effect transport is its own later lane, deliberately uncoupled. The mechanical sweep exists (curated_cargo_probe_one.sh spine); 16-entry stratified sample first, full 744 sweep wide on srvN (~2–4h) → per-entry first-error TSV = the enrollment census, whose first-error classes become the EmitIneligible refusal vocabulary."),
          authored(id: "ts-native-seams", done: false, content: "**executor seams** — family cold-build as a scheduled node the governor prices separately from member runs; per-witness leg attribution in floor receipts (native family/member vs interpreted — without it the flip is unobservable); typed EmitIneligible first-error refusal rows so residue is a prioritized list, never a silent skip. Crate grain is measurement-settled (#6879): per-witness LOSES (~17s cargo apiece); one-corpus-crate barred by real fn-name collisions; ~15–30 family crates clustered by shared closure, durable via GUNBC_NATIVE_CACHE_ROOT so srvN pays each cold build approximately once ever."),
          authored(id: "ts-native-flip", done: false, content: "**the bulk flip PR — one PR, three sections**: (1) census as data — all 744 entries classified on the routing frontier, no entry unlisted (totality wall), rows landed in DERIVED Group form (DeclarationRef subjects, closure-derived membership — never 744 fresh string nicknames; group 5a); (2) the executor seams; (3) the disposition flip with the in-PR agreement receipt and the falsifier cold control untouched. Expected effect: the ~30-min interpreter leg shrinks toward the residue share (~10% host-fed + sweep-named ineligibles); family builds amortize to ~zero on the durable cache."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-native-census"), parent: nid(s: "ts-native-bulk") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-native-seams"), parent: nid(s: "ts-native-bulk") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-native-flip"), parent: nid(s: "ts-native-bulk") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "3 · Work intake — dispatch from the roadmap, not ad hoc",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-dispatch-elevate", done: false, content: "**roadmap-driven dispatch — the machinery is LANDED; three gaps to go-live (assessed 2026-07-22)**: `gunbc serve` on srv1 serves the LIVE roadmap with `POST /dispatch/NODE_ID` invoking `belt_dispatch_node` in-process; the belt observes fail-closed (tmux ls), reconciles the ready frontier, and spawns `git worktree add` + tmux running claude with the FILLED dispatch brief as appended system prompt (effort mapped from node Intricacy), deterministic session UUID, typed refusals throughout; `belt_run_once_json` is the CLI tick for receipts. Gaps: (1) TREE FRESHNESS — srv1's tree/binary have been stale since belt B merged because every deploy failed; unblocks with the first green deploy post-#7086; (2) ONE LIVE END-TO-END RECEIPT — never collected with real claude (tests used a fake): ssh srv1, run belt_run_once_json once, converge whatever typed refusals it names (likely tmux/claude/claude-auth for the service user); (3) SIZED NODES — dispatchability requires intricacy/volume + Accept line + deps-done; the task-sheet authored() rows are unsized tracking rows BY DESIGN, so size the lane nodes you actually want dispatched. Auth precondition: 3b's dispatch-auth row before the button is exposed beyond the tailnet."),
          authored(id: "ts-intake-discipline", done: false, content: "**until the actuator lands, this sheet is the intake queue** — new work enters as a row here or as a sized lane node with an Accept line, never ad hoc mid-session; dispatch top-down by the numbering; a session that discovers work files a row instead of chasing it."),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "3b · Access + compute fabric — no hidden transport dependencies (operator, 2026-07-22)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-access-model", done: false, content: "**access is currently a transport accident, not a model** — the dashboard's only wall is tailnet membership (the unit binds 0.0.0.0:8080, so any LAN peer reaches it; `POST /dispatch/NODE_ID` spawns a permission-skipping claude session with NO auth of its own), and the tailnet is the operator's personal one — a hidden dependency of exactly the class the operator ruled against. Holistic shape: model access as grants on the compute fabric — tailscale is FINE as a realization, but it must be a MODELED access pattern (who can reach which serving surface / press which actuation) with the transport as one handler, never the implicit wall. Grounds in the visibility-grants thread (`Publish` verb, AudienceScopeTree) and effect-grants (verb × subtree admission on the dispatch route); the belt's own note already names the destination ('nicer later as compute fabric', operator 2026-07-18)."),
          authored(id: "ts-access-orgtailnet", done: false, content: "**org tailnet** — operator creates it (not done yet, 2026-07-22); repo side = re-point `fleet_intent_network.tailnet_domain` from the personal tailnet and model the tailnet as a cited access realization row, the same personal→infra decoupling as retiring `service_user: briansrls`. Until then srv1.tailecbe08.ts.net stands, and the LAN IP:port works for the operator directly (the unit already binds 0.0.0.0)."),
          authored(id: "ts-access-dispatch-auth", done: false, content: "**dispatch actuation auth is a go-live precondition** — before the Dispatch button matters, who can press it must be a modeled fact: the POST route gains its own admission check (grant-based, audience-scoped), never inherits whatever the network provides. Do NOT drop the tailscale front before this lands — it is the only wall in front of an actuation endpoint."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-access-orgtailnet"), parent: nid(s: "ts-access-model") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-access-dispatch-auth"), parent: nid(s: "ts-access-model") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "3a · The stabilization loop — why item 3 exists (receipts)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-loop-pattern", done: false, content: "**name the loop: CI hurts → quick patch at the symptom layer → the patch regresses something else → repeat** — the instances below are receipts, not blame lines; the common shape is a fix landed under pressure without its own red-control, verified against a CI that was itself too slow or too red to check it (and merged before its verdict landed). The house rules already cover this (§5 factory model — analyze the stopped line before restart; §6 — root-cause, never fork-patch); the ask is that the loop's next iteration goes through a lane with a receipt instead of another hotfix, starting with the acute rows above."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-prepush", done: true, content: "pre-push hooks grew a CI-scale artifact/witness gate because CI was slow → local pushes broke and stalled → #7076 right-sized the hook back down (MERGED 2026-07-22)."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-fmt", done: true, content: "nextest (37 GiB, red on main) removed from CI 2026-07-11 with fmt riding along, coverage claimed by the pre-push hook → the hook is absent in fresh clones → a fmt violation landed on main (#6658) → fmt re-enrolled as a standalone fast gate (#6691)."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-docsonly", done: true, content: "docs-only skip added for speed → silently bypassed the whole witness corpus including the doc-graph wall → retired #7023/#7039; docs-only PRs now run normal selection."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-falsifier", done: false, content: "affected-set selection made PRs fast → corpus-read witnesses predict-skip → the falsifier ran red 29+ consecutive times unnoticed → falsifier-alert #7022 made it loud → the roster burn-down landed with this sheet update; the exit is the next scheduled green."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-buildretry", done: false, content: "the release-build step's EAGAIN retry ladder (jobs=1, then drop RUSTC_WRAPPER) keeps builds green while masking the sccache/host deficit — the srvN build-cache provisioning lane owns the root fix (DESIGN open thread; STEP 2 fallback removal is operator-sequenced after T4)."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-stale-roster", done: true, content: "#7060 moved a witness to the long lane but left its explicit roster row enrolled → every main run red for ~3 hours (no-main-function-found) → hotfix #7079; enrollment-vs-definition living in two places is the same single-authority class the unconsumed-component row names."),
          authored(id: "ts-loop-deploy", done: false, content: "deploy-to-srv1 folded into the ci run for CD → srv1 host state now reds main daily independent of code health — the deploy-tail row above is the acute half; the CD-transport §2 node is the root."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-prepush"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-fmt"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-docsonly"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-falsifier"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-buildretry"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-deploy"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-loop-stale-roster"), parent: nid(s: "ts-loop-pattern") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "4 · Antagonistic product review — the last two weeks of merges",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-review-sweep", done: false, content: "**sweep the ~300 PRs merged since 2026-07-15 with the operator's checklist (authored 2026-07-22)**: does this PR accomplish what it was supposed to? if not, what remains? what issues happened? what context should pass to the next session? Output = per-PR disposition rows (finish · consume · revert · accept); prioritize merges whose mechanisms have zero executing consumers, and merges landed while the falsifier was dark (2026-07-16 onward — the whole wave)."),
          authored(id: "ts-concat-class", done: false, content: "**the concat-composition class — shortcuts that calcify and spread** — string-building `concat` chains as the easiest path to the objective: 2,798 `concat(` sites in dag+src/v2, 112 nested `concat(concat(` in dag/** alone, densest in host/shell-adjacent modules (`srv3_os_install_reconcile_receipt` · `host_build_cache_provision` · `cli_invoke`) — exactly where the shell→intent rework fights them, and visible in open PRs now. The ruling already exists (operator 2026-07-14, #6656: a string literal is an ATOM, never a COMPOSITION; `TargetText` carrier at the emit seam) — the work is the census + wall: classify each chain (emit-seam-internal = fine · smuggled composition = migrate to its typed carrier) and gate new ones at the boundary so the class stops spreading."),
          authored(id: "ts-unconsumed", done: false, content: "**unconsumed-component sweep** — mechanisms merged without an executing consumer are coverage-by-illusion (§6); the admission invariant (every witness row names an executing consumer — module-identity thread Phase 0) is the wall. Sweep the wave for landed-but-inert mechanisms and either wire a consumer or revert."),
          authored(id: "ts-sustainable-close", done: false, content: "**redefine done for PRs — finishing the task is not finishing the work**: a PR closes sustainably when the antagonistic review passes AND the modeling audit (item 5) passes AND its context-for-next-session lands on the carrier (item 6), not in the chat."),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "4a · Open-PR audit — disposition every open PR (12 at snapshot)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-pr-audit", done: false, content: "**audit the remaining open PRs and decide each one's disposition** — merge · review-then-merge · fold into another lane · close; the 12 open at snapshot (16:30 UTC) are the children below; re-sweep after the merge wave settles, applying item 4's checklist and item 5's modeling audit to each."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7080", done: true, content: "#7080 layering gate false edges — the reference-derived producer misattributed prelude bare names, binders, and record-literal labels as cross-layer import edges (the one floor red left after #7082); fix verified pre-merge by a local red/green pair (gate witness false on main's tree, true with the PR applied, same tree same witness) — MERGED 2026-07-22 (7c222fc). Also the enabler for closure-derived Group<U> membership (group 5a)."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7078", done: false, content: "#7078 §13 alias APPLY as `.dag` workflow (`session/fierce-crab-363`) — ready; clean vs main, no generated artifacts touched, honest placeholder discipline (its equivalence witness is a self-declared scaffold, not the dual-run gate); Rust plan side retained until the real dual-run equivalence receipt."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7077", done: true, content: "#7077 srv1 deploy readiness fix (was mistitled `dag roadmap work`) — poll bound 30s→120s grounded in measurement: four srv1 starts listening at 35–39s against a 30s bound, so every prior deploy red was the probe quitting ~4s early on a successful start; expectation (40s) and bound (×3 margin) split into separate decls with the demand-scoped-load dissolution trigger — MERGED 2026-07-22 (fec005aa). Residual: `witness_poll_max_attempts_is_thirty` now asserts 120 — rename on next touch."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7076", done: true, content: "#7076 right-size the emitted pre-push hook — CI-scale artifact drift gate dropped from GitPrePushHook — MERGED 2026-07-22 (d50e25b)."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7074", done: true, content: "#7074 cli_run.rs hollowing ledger — CLOSED by operator 2026-07-22, reframed as roadmap description: the census stands as the drain map (867 fns; LensHostBridge 225 + NamespaceResolutionSymbolIndex 214 + AffectedSetSelection 141 = 580/867 — two-thirds of the file on two v2 lanes), while the Python generator and its §3 second-producer question dissolve with the PR. Seed management continues in group 7."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7072", done: true, content: "#7072 finish #7043 floor budget refusal on FloorOutcome + plan-roster fact (`session/tidy-ibex-424`) — MERGED 2026-07-22 (44e538d)."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7069", done: false, content: "#7069 CI onto v2 — routing frontier + parity gate + consumption P4/P2/R1/R2 (`session/native-routing-consumption`) — operator merging 2026-07-22 after rebase+regen (ci.yml drift collision with the heal merges). Parity windows DEMOTED from flip-precondition to post-flip monitoring (operator re-pricing 2026-07-22: no customers — prefer immediate loud divergence over drip-feed); R2 toolchain-identity key rides its commit 4. Immediate follow-on so it does not pile up: the family re-key row (group 5a); opens the bulk-native arc (group 2a)."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7068", done: true, content: "#7068 dissolve cssl_emit_artifact_sanitize v1_rt-strip — dead rule deleted, pub-use-dedupe gap named for crisp-fox-839 — MERGED 2026-07-22 (46127b9)."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7066", done: false, content: "#7066 Gate-1 receipt lane B1 — modeled per-module behavioral-receipt producer (`session/nimble-deer-372`) — template body; brief pending."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7058", done: true, content: "#7058 post-merge honest frontier re-sweep — generic-T dead, type-ref-import-missing named successor class (`session/sharp-bee-290-roadmap-converge`) — MERGED 2026-07-22 (e89f076); its main run is the first to exercise the deploy tail with both unit fixes in tree."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7050", done: false, content: "#7050 computation-identity de-fork census R1–R8 (`session/computation-identity-defork`) — doc + bind row only, clean vs main; merge. R2 (durable native cache toolchain identity) now lands via #7069 commit 4 — the census row stays as its receipt."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7027", done: false, content: "#7027 srv4 BMC onboarding G1–G4 — parameterize per-host, gcloud self-provision, operator-token handler (`session/srv4-onboarding-credential-rotation-gap`) — ready; unblocks srv4."),
          authored(id: "ts-pr-7008", done: true, content: "#7008 Phase-A design-library lift — gunbc.design.* extraction + census frontier — MERGED 2026-07-22 (cadb472)."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-pr-7080"), parent: nid(s: "ts-pr-audit") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-pr-7078"), parent: nid(s: "ts-pr-audit") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-pr-7077"), parent: nid(s: "ts-pr-audit") },
