          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-pr-7008"), parent: nid(s: "ts-pr-audit") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "5 · Modeling audit — a standing pass, not a one-off",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-modeling-pass", done: false, content: "**per-PR modeling questions**: what models does this add — and should it add more? any anemic leaves (a `String` hiding named parts, a bare alias, an Option meaning three things)? does each new concept ground in an existing authority or mint a nickname (§2/§3)? Run it on the wave's merges alongside item 4's sweep; the §3 enforcement-intent lane's model-quality consumers (anemia/consolidation, node E) are its mechanization."),
          authored(id: "ts-standing-intent", done: false, content: "**model items 4+5 as StandingIntent rows — ask once, compile forever** — the antagonistic-review checklist and the modeling-audit questions are operator standing directives being re-paid each conversation; DESIGN's enforcement-intent thread exists precisely to make them durable gated rows (intent ⇄ LensContract ⇄ coverage receipt). Until that lands, both checklists live HERE as the review template for every PR close."),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "5a · Group of units — pluralities get standard representations (operator, 2026-07-22)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-group-u", done: false, content: "**a group of units is never a nickname** — taxonomy by how membership is KNOWN: positional (containment — module, the gold standard: being-in IS being-there, wrong membership unwritable) · derived (a computed relation — closure reachability, inhabitance, measured cost: membership is a query) · frontier (asserted per-row WITH reason + dissolve-on — sanctioned countable debt, the self-host-frontier shape) · nickname (asserted, string-keyed, no trigger — the violation; `family: String` and the closed #7074 feature enum are the type specimens). Migration pipeline: mint → frontier → query. Formalization home is the enforcement-intent carrier (its subject_roster IS this concept — no new lane): register every unit-naming roster; the gate = each registered group is Derived or Frontier-with-trigger; a bare unit-naming List of strings outside the registry is a review reject; a storage-grain proxy (dir/substring membership) must name its construction backstop (the long/ lane's 5s eval deadline is the blessed example — the dir cannot lie) or convert to Frontier rows."),
          authored(id: "ts-group-family", done: false, content: "**family re-key — the immediate #7069 follow-on (operator: figure out where this dissolves immediately, else these pile up)**: `family: String` → the subject construct's DeclarationRef; membership derived as closure-reaches-subject from the EXISTING closure authority — needs no namespace terminal (#7080's false-edge fix was the blocker and is on main; the containment SymbolIndex re-points the derivation later as a one-projection swap). Precondition for the bulk flip PR (2a) landing its 744 rows Derived rather than as 744 fresh nicknames."),
          authored(id: "ts-group-census", done: false, content: "**the census to burn down (swept 2026-07-22)**: `witness_exclusion_substrings` + its offline/fixture projections (highest churn; its own note already declares the dissolve — rows carry derived consumer classification and the parallel lists delete) · the lens exception rosters (meta_exec_confinement · realization_vocab · inert_carrier · complexity_linearity_migration_debt · lens_registry_completeness) → typed Frontier rows, their prose reasons becoming typed fields · NON_FOLD_RESIDUE_ROSTER re-homed from cli_run.rs onto a .dag carrier (couples to group 7 data-out) · discovery_scan_dirs / pool_roots (storage-grain proxies needing declared backstops). Burn down opportunistically when a PR touches the neighborhood; new instances blocked at review by the ts-group-u rule."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-group-family"), parent: nid(s: "ts-group-u") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-group-census"), parent: nid(s: "ts-group-u") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "6 · Planning + documentation — the stable anchor",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-doc-anchor", done: false, content: "**every session starts and ends at a carrier, not a chat** — sessions drift context (more goldfish than they appear); the plan doc / lane node is the stable anchor with explicit expectations. So: dispatch always seeds from a brief bound to a plan (`dispatch_brief_template`, item 3); work-in-progress marks land on the carrier just-in-time (DESIGN §6 — the mark IS the authority, no parallel ledgers); and item 4's context-to-pass-forward question writes back to the plan doc at close. Existing machinery to lean on: the plan registry (#7012 — the registered PlanArtifact IS the doc binding) and the md↔dag delta-first thread."),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "7 · Seed interim — cli_run.rs managed, not generated (yet)",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-seed-interim", done: false, content: "**cli_run.rs cannot be generated from .dag today, and pretending otherwise is the specification-without-execution trap** — it IS the host seam (filesystem · git · process · cgroups · CLI), exactly the effect-transport layer the emitter learns last (the same fact that caps the native corpus at ~90%, group 2a). Receipt for why interim management is needed NOW: 26,686 lines, 988 fns; +2,747/−629 across 16 commits in the 33h of the merge wave — the §7 seed that should shrink toward zero grew ~8% in a day and a half, unpriced and invisible per-PR, and the operator observes the dumping ACCELERATES as v2 nears. The bulk-native arc (2a) is the biggest single hollowing step available; the rows below stop the inflow and move the movable."),
          authored(id: "ts-seed-ratchet", done: false, content: "**growth ratchet as a gate (§5 construction, not vigilance)**: cli_run.rs fn count becomes a floor receipt; growth is admissible only with a declared SeedGrowthJustification row (reason + owning dissolution lane — the frontier pattern applied to the seed itself). Every dump becomes a counted decision instead of an invisible default."),
          authored(id: "ts-seed-data-out", done: false, content: "**data out now (zero emitter work, real shrink)**: rosters living in Rust move to .dag carriers the host reads — NON_FOLD_RESIDUE_ROSTER (its reasons + dissolve triggers become typed fields, group 5a); the exclusion-list mirror whose own note says it must stay byte-identical to the .dag authority (a live §3 dual representation — single-source it, host reads through)."),
          authored(id: "ts-seed-intake", done: false, content: "**intake policy**: new host capability lands as extdeps interface shape + a THIN generic transport (the host_effect_apply funnel, per the shell→intent routing authority) — a cli_run fn carrying business logic rather than a transport shim is a review reject. Most of the wave's +2.7k lines had a .dag home available; the ratchet row makes this checkable rather than aspirational."),
        ],
        edges: [
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-seed-ratchet"), parent: nid(s: "ts-seed-interim") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-seed-data-out"), parent: nid(s: "ts-seed-interim") },
          RoadmapEdge { child: nid(s: "ts-seed-intake"), parent: nid(s: "ts-seed-interim") },
        ],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "Session branches running CI with no open PR at snapshot",
        nodes: [
          authored(id: "ts-branches", done: false, content: "**each should end as a PR row above or be abandoned deliberately** — `session/sunny-owl-513` (deploy tree-sync fix) · `session/swift-eagle-602` (layering-imports gate P1) · `session/merry-heron-629` (#6985 witness-discovery cascade: pullable() misses arity-zero bare refs) · `session/sleek-crab-621` (fleet_show systemctl via typed extdeps op) · `session/bright-heron-200-work` (exclusion-lane strict-walk closure) · `session/nimble-moth-292-6939` (typed-cache: reference-derived import term in the content key) · `docs/namespace-y-readjudication` (namespace §4 re-adjudication) · `fix/tidy-ibex-merge` (governor fix)."),
        ],
        edges: [],
